---
title: Pumpkin Spice Bars
course: Dessert
tags: 
- Bars
- Vegan
source: Modified from The Cookie Book
cuisine: American
servings: 50
---

Preheat an oven to 350.

For bars, in a #large mixing bowl{} stir together the @all-purpose flour{310%g}, @brown sugar{100%g}, @sugar{100%g}, @baking powder{2.5%tsp}, @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, @ground ginger{1/2%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp}. In a #medium mixing bowl{}, stir the @plant-based milk{80%g}, @canned pumpkin{250%g}, @raisins{140%g}, and @vegetable oil{120%ml}. Stir the pumpkin mixture into the flour mixture.

Spread the batte into a 15 x 10 x 1-inch (37.5 x 25 x 2.5-cm) #baking pan{} lined with parchment paper. Bake for ~{15-20%minutes}, or until a wooden toothpick or fine skewer inserted near the center comes out clean. Cool in the pan on a wire rack.

For topping, in a #small, heavy-duty plastic bag{} combine the @white chocolate, chopped{90%g} and @vegan butter{1%tsp}. Close the bag just above the ingredients, then set the sealed bag in a bowl of warm water until the contents are melted.

Snip 1/4 inch (6 mm) from one corner of the bag. Squeeze the topping from the bag over the bars in a crisscross design. Cut the bars into small squares before the topping is completely set. 